<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's AutoEuropa boosting output 20 pct 1996.</title>
<headline>Portugal's AutoEuropa boosting output 20 pct 1996.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>AutoEuropa, the Volkswagen-Ford, joint venture in Portugal, expects to boost its output of passenger vans by some 20 percent to 121,000 vehicles in 1996, a company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Output stood at 81,305 vehicles at the end of August.</p>
<p>According to a report in the Diario Economico newspaper, Germany will take some 41 percent of the production, followed by the U.K. with 13.9 percent and France with 13 percent.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
